Cell["\<\
The five main inputs have a direct physical meaning: lattice and lattpar \
define the Bravais lattice, wyckoffposition specifies the inequivalent sites \
and their moments, symminformation gives the symmetry operations, and \
basisFunctions specifies the local orbital space on each Wyckoff orbit.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5958d390-901b-4665-91bf-61cce581a927"],

Cell["\<\
After init finishes, first inspect the generated atoms, the orbital order, \
and the neighbour shells. The hopping parameters are not needed at this \
stage; symham determines them later, one shell at a time.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"25b3ed17-dd09-4b0a-b216-5ddc47776fd9"],

Cell["\<\
By default init finds the first 10 complete bond shells. If a model needs a \
farther shell, choose a larger InitialBondShells value and run init again; \
symham itself does not search for new bonds.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"07a7d3d4-f4c6-49b5-aff7-3ceee259a992"],

Cell["\<\
RepresentationMode selects how the full orbital representation is built. Use \
\"DirectProduct\" when the action on the complete local basis is known, and \
\"Induced\" when the input starts from a representation of a site-symmetry \
group.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7b06267e-d86d-45c9-82ff-62049f860026"],

Cell["\<\
Every call to init starts a new model. If the input is inconsistent, the \
calculation stops and asks the user to correct it; MagneticTB does not \
silently continue with the preceding model.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"cd38b79a-2241-4d48-a84d-2f7d35fffcf0"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "dcada8f4-7863-414d-9698-48758024e17e"], "lattice", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"a", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "a"}], "/", "2"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "3", "]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"a", "/", "2"}]}], ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "c"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], Cell["\<\
Primitive direct-lattice vectors stored by rows. After applying lattpar, the \
result must be a real, nonsingular numerical 3 by 3 matrix.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"0778be80-a611-4611-94c8-f33d3c95eb71"]},
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "7340a0d0-7277-4a64-82b8-f7e4d5858c64"], "lattpar", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"a", "->", "1"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"c", "->", "3"}]}], "}"}], Cell["\<\
Replacement rules that assign numerical values to every symbolic lattice \
parameter needed by lattice.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"88d57ea7-455d-4a20-a8b3-79bbead1e094"]},
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "5ec90758-0f26-4ffa-888f-0ee1928f4a4c"], "wyckoffposition", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"2", "/", "3"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "3"}], ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", 
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "}"}], Cell["\<\
One {fractional seed position, magnetic moment} pair for each Wyckoff orbit. \
The outer-list order also fixes the order of basisFunctions.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"a9a7e91a-056c-47f8-b8d0-853e56e495ae"]},
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "425220dc-f68d-4896-8a2c-527a826c1913"], "symminformation", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<1\>\"", ",", 
       RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", "\"\<F\>\""}], "}"}], 
     "}"}], Cell["\<\
Either ordered magnetic-group records {label,R,t,\"F\"|\"T\"} or a discrete \
spin-space-group Association. The antiunitary flag belongs to each operation \
record.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"e7724be7-c71a-41ec-8370-812a7dddf394"]},
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "8b3afa9a-540d-4508-be7f-74b9301af91f"], "basisFunctions", 
    RowBox[{"{", "\"\<s\>\"", "}"}], Cell["\<\
A nonempty local scalar-orbital or two-component spinor basis for every \
Wyckoff seed. Named orbitals and exact symbolic functions are accepted.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"552eee16-24b4-4e32-ba26-46798195d1d3"]},
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "897b8c63-5938-4197-b034-f1bcc0d8a884"], "InitialBondShells", "10", 
    Cell["\<\
Number of complete bond shells found during initialization. Shell 1 contains \
the zero-distance onsite terms; shell 2 is the first nonzero-distance \
neighbour shell.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"34c97e95-ed12-4c9c-a4cc-2116a89228dc"]},
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "da0bab41-8833-4839-a891-40ca6b31ab20"], "GenerateSymmetryGroup", 
    "False", Cell["\<\
False treats the supplied ordered records as the complete finite group. True \
closes supplied generators using the operation-specific multiplication law.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"fbb9aa8b-69b0-49b0-b6a1-ff07842dba7d"]},
   {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon",ExpressionUUID->
     "c1a117d8-1257-4756-9d2e-e1b301657d54"], 
    "RepresentationMode", "\"\<DirectProduct\>\"", Cell["\<\
\"DirectProduct\" uses the local action on the full basis together with the \
permutation of equivalent sites. \"Induced\" derives the reference-site \
representation from basisFunctions and transports it to the other sites. Use \
initfromrep when exact site-symmetry matrices are already known.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"679bb0b2-9b6e-451d-b914-b5a40cd10656"]}
  },
  GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
  GridBoxDividers->{"Rows" -> {{False}}},
  GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {
      Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
       Offset[0.7]}, 
      Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "Rows" -> {
      Offset[0.2], {
       Offset[0.8]}, 
      Offset[0.2]}}]], "3ColumnTableMod",
 GridBoxOptions->{
 GridBoxBackground->{
  "Columns" -> {{None}}, 
   "Rows" -> {None, None, None, None, None, None, None, {None}}},
 GridBoxDividers->{
  "Rows" -> {{
     True, True, True, True, True, True, True, True, 
      True}}}},ExpressionUUID->"209c5f44-9153-4dc3-98f3-9552be77a9d0"]
}, Closed]],

